ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE HOUSING SITE DEVELOPMENT PROMOTION ACT

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters necessary for enforcing the Housing Site Development Promotion Act.

Article 2 (Scope of public facilities)
"Facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 2, subparagraph 2 of the Housing Site Development Promotion Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means the following facilities: <Amended on 2015.11.11, 2020.12.8, 2024.7.2>
1. Children's playgrounds, senior citizens' centers, assembly halls (including community halls) and other facilities used for the convenience of residential life, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
2. Deleted. <2015.11.11>
3. The following facilities necessary to secure self-sufficiency of an area:
(a) Sales facilities, business facilities, medical facilities, distribution facilities and other facilities deemed necessary for the welfare of residents by the designating authority under Article 3-2;
(b) The following facilities for regional development and job creation:
  (1) Venture business cluster facilities under Article 2 (4) of the Special Act on the Promotion of Venture Businesses;
  (2) Urban-type factories under Article 28 of the Industrial Cluster Development and Factory Establishment Act;
  (3) Software promotion facilities under Article 11 of the Software Promotion Act;
  (4) Other facilities similar to those under items (1) through (3), as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
(c) Facilities for hotel businesses under Article 3 (1) 2 (a) of the Tourism Promotion Act;
(d) Cultural and assembly facilities listed in attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
(e) Education and research facilities listed in attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
(f) Agricultural facilities, including horticultural facilities, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
(g) Other facilities necessary to secure regional self-sufficiency as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
4. Facilities for managing public facilities, etc.

Article 2-2 (Designation of housing site development districts)
① "Scale prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 3 (2) of the Act means 3,300,000 square meters.
② "Scale prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 3 (3) 3 of the Act means 1,000,000 square meters.

Article 3 (Changes to minor matters)
"Cases of changing minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 3 (4) of the Act means any of the following: Provided, That in the case of subparagraph 2, where the area proposed to be added to a housing site development district is an area determined and publicly notified as subject to reclamation under Article 13 of the Rearrangement of Agricultural and Fishing Villages Act, a protection area for military bases and installations designated under Article 4 of the Protection of Military Bases and Installations Act, or where farmland is newly included in the area to be added, the heads of relevant central administrative agencies (or heads of relevant administrative agencies in the case of a Special Self-Governing Province; hereinafter the same shall apply) shall be consulted in advance:
1. Reduction of the area of a housing site development district;
2. Expansion of the area of a housing site development district by not more than ten percent.

Article 3-2 (Consultation on designation of housing site development districts)
The head of a relevant central administrative agency or local government requested to consult or provide an opinion concerning designation of a housing site development district under Article 3 (4) of the Act by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, a Special Metropolitan Mayor, Metropolitan Mayor, Do Governor or Special Self-Governing Province Governor (hereinafter referred to as the "designating authority") shall present an opinion within 30 days from receipt of the request.

Article 4 Deleted. <2007.7.30>

Article 4-2 (Proposals for designation of housing site development districts)
① A person falling under any of Article 7 (1) 1 through 4 of the Act who intends to propose designation of a housing site development district to the designating authority under Article 3-2 of the Act shall submit the proposal together with:
1. A survey report on the housing site development district under Article 4 of the Act;
2. A location map at a scale of 1:25,000;
3. A topographic map at a scale of 1:5,000 indicating the boundaries of the district and the reasons for their determination;
4. Documents showing the current status of the city;
5. Survey materials concerning farmland and forest land included in the district;
6. Photographs of current conditions;
7. Materials concerning metropolitan transportation systems around the housing site development district (limited to districts of at least the area prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport);
8. Materials prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport as necessary for environmental review.
② On receipt of a proposal under paragraph ①, the designating authority shall verify cadastral and forest land maps through the joint use of administrative information under Article 36 (1) of the Electronic Government Act.
③ Where a registered business operator under Article 4 of the Housing Act (hereinafter referred to as a "housing construction business operator") and a person falling under Article 7 (1) 1 through 3 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "public project implementer") intend to jointly implement a housing site development project under Article 7 (1) 4 of the Act, they shall jointly propose designation of the district. <Amended on 2016.8.11>
④ A housing site development district proposed for designation under Article 3-2 of the Act shall have an area of at least 100,000 square meters: Provided, That persons jointly proposing designation under paragraph ③ may propose designation in any of the following cases: <Amended on 2014.4.29, 2015.12.22>
1. An urban area under Article 36 (1) 1 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act (hereinafter referred to as an "urban area") with a proposed district of at least 10,000 square meters: Provided, That where the proposed district is less than 30,000 square meters, this shall be limited to cases where construction of public housing under Article 2, subparagraph 1 of the Special Act on Public Housing Construction, etc. (hereinafter referred to as "public housing") is urgently necessary on the portion of housing construction land corresponding to the public project implementer's share to alleviate housing shortages in urban areas;
2. An area outside urban areas with a proposed district of at least 30,000 square meters;
3. A case recognized by a public project implementer as especially necessary for public housing construction, etc. following deliberation by the Housing Policy Deliberation Committee under Article 8 of the Framework Act on Residence.
⑤ Persons intending to propose designation under paragraphs ① and ③ shall formulate and implement security management measures to prevent disclosure of related information in the course of investigations and consultations for the proposed designation.

Article 5 (Hearing opinions of residents, etc.)
① Where the designating authority (excluding a Special Self-Governing Province Governor; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article) intends to hear the opinions of residents and relevant experts concerning designation of a housing site development district under Article 3-3 of the Act, it shall send copies of relevant documents to the head of the competent Si or Gun or the head of the autonomous Gu.
② Where a Special Self-Governing Province Governor intends to hear the opinions of residents and relevant experts under Article 3-3 of the Act, or the head of a Si, Gun or autonomous Gu receives relevant documents under paragraph ①, the Governor or head shall promptly announce the name, location, area, etc. of the proposed district. The documents shall be made available for public inspection for 14 days from the date of announcement.
③ A person having an opinion concerning designation of a housing site development district may submit a written opinion to the Special Self-Governing Province Governor or the head of the Si, Gun or autonomous Gu during the inspection period under paragraph ②.
④ Where opinions are submitted under paragraph ③, the head of the Si, Gun or autonomous Gu shall compile them and submit them to the designating authority, or notify the authority that no opinions were submitted.
⑤ "Minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 3-3 (1) of the Act means matters falling under any subparagraph of Article 3.
⑥ Notwithstanding paragraph ①, the designating authority may directly hear the opinions of residents and relevant experts if:
1. The proposed housing site development district extends across two or more Sis, Guns or autonomous Gus;
2. The head of a Si, Gun or autonomous Gu receiving relevant documents under paragraph ① fails to make an announcement under paragraph ②.
⑦ Where the designating authority hears opinions under paragraph ⑥, paragraphs ② through ④ shall apply mutatis mutandis; a residents' briefing or public hearing shall be held at least once during the inspection period, and the name, location, area, etc. of the proposed district shall be announced in the Official Gazette.

Article 6 (Acts subject to permission)
① Acts requiring permission from the competent Special Self-Governing Province Governor or head of a Si, Gun or autonomous Gu under Article 6 (1) of the Act shall be: <Amended on 2021.1.5>
1. Construction, etc. of buildings: Construction, substantial repair or change of use of a building under Article 2 (1) 2 of the Building Act (including temporary buildings);
2. Installation of structures: Installation of man-made structures other than buildings under Article 2 (1) 2 of the Building Act;
3. Change of the form and quality of land: Altering the shape of land by cutting, filling, leveling, paving, etc., excavation of land or reclamation of public waters;
4. Extraction of soil and stone: Extracting earth, sand, gravel, rocks, etc.; extraction for the purpose of changing the form and quality of land shall be governed by subparagraph 3;
5. Subdivision of land;
6. Stacking objects: Stacking objects not easily movable for at least one month;
7. Cutting and planting trees.
② Where a Special Self-Governing Province Governor or the head of a Si, Gun or autonomous Gu intends to grant permission for an act under the subparagraphs of paragraph ① pursuant to Article 6 (1) of the Act and a housing site development project implementer (hereinafter referred to as a "project implementer") has been designated under Article 7 of the Act, the Governor or head shall hear that implementer's opinion in advance.
③ "Acts prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 6 (2) 2 of the Act means the following acts that are not subject to development activity permission under Article 56 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act:
1. Installation of simple structures directly used to produce agricultural, forestry or fishery products, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
2. Changes in the form and quality of land for cultivation;
3. Extraction of soil and stone to the extent that it does not impede development of the housing site development district or damage natural landscapes;
4. Stacking objects on land that has been determined to remain in the housing site development district;
5. Temporary planting of ornamental trees (excluding temporary planting on cultivated land).
④ A person required to report under Article 6 (3) of the Act shall submit a report to the competent Special Self-Governing Province Governor or head of a Si, Gun or autonomous Gu within 30 days from designation and public notification of the district, accompanied by the status of construction or project progress and the implementation plan.

Article 6-2 (Requirements for joint public-private housing site development projects)
① "Ratio prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 7 (1) 4 of the Act means:
1. Where a public project implementer requests a housing construction business operator to jointly implement a housing site development project as determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport: 20 percent;
2. Where a housing construction business operator requests a public project implementer to jointly implement a housing site development project to overcome difficulties in acquiring land or obtaining project plan approval, etc.: 50 percent.
② A housing construction business operator seeking joint implementation with a public project implementer under Article 7 (1) 4 of the Act shall meet any of the following requirements: <Amended on 2016.8.11>
1. Having registered under Article 9 of the Framework Act on the Construction Industry in a business category conducting general construction works (limited to building construction or civil engineering and building construction);
2. Meeting the standards under Article 7 of the Housing Act;
3. Having concluded a contract for housing construction works with a person falling under subparagraph 1.
③ By the time an agreement is concluded under Article 6-3 (3), a housing construction business operator shall own land or have concluded agreements to transfer ownership of land in an amount at least equal to the ratio under paragraph ①. Ownership of land subject to such agreements shall be acquired before the relevant housing site development district is designated.

Article 6-3 (Procedures for implementing joint public-private housing site development projects)
① A housing construction business operator intending to request joint implementation of a housing site development project from a public project implementer shall submit a specific project plan covering the boundaries of the housing site development district, development directions, housing construction plans, etc.
② Where a housing construction business operator requests joint implementation, the public project implementer shall determine whether to accept the request, considering public interest, commercial feasibility, etc., as determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, and notify the requesting operator of the determination within 30 days from receipt of the request. Where the request is rejected, reasons shall be specified.
③ A housing construction business operator and a public project implementer intending to implement a joint housing site development project shall enter into an agreement including:
1. Scope and scale of the project;
2. Scope and division of duties;
3. Transfer of ownership of land, etc.;
4. Installation and management of public facilities, etc.;
5. Installation of infrastructure and allocation of costs;
6. Settlement of expenses where the public project implementer uses as housing sites land secured by the housing construction business operator;
7. Other matters deemed necessary by the housing construction business operator or public project implementer.
④ When the operator and public project implementer jointly propose designation of a housing site development district to the designating authority under Article 4-2 (3), they shall submit the agreement under paragraph ③ in addition to the documents specified in the subparagraphs of Article 4-2 (1). The designating authority shall verify cadastral maps and forest land maps through the joint use of administrative information under Article 36 (1) of the Electronic Government Act.
⑤ Among housing sites developed through a joint project, the housing construction business operator shall directly use for housing construction, etc. the sites corresponding to its share (meaning sites used by that operator under Article 9-2): Provided, That where the operator finds it difficult to apply for approval of a housing construction project plan under Article 15 of the Housing Act within two years from the date of approval of the implementation plan under Article 9 (1) of the Act due to bankruptcy, insolvency or other circumstances, it may request the public project implementer to purchase the sites at development cost. <Amended on 2016.8.11>

Article 6-4 (Methods for selecting housing construction business operators by public project implementers)
① A public project implementer shall select housing construction business operators through open competitive solicitation under Article 7 (1) 5 of the Act.
② An agreement concluded by a public project implementer with a housing construction business operator shall include:
1. Scope and scale of the project, including its name, location, area and period;
2. Scope and allocation of duties between the public project implementer and the housing construction business operator;
3. Project costs and financing plans;
4. Amendments to project plans;
5. Supply and disposal of developed housing sites;
6. Profit ratio of the housing construction business operator;
7. Installation of infrastructure and sharing of expenses;
8. Transfer and follow-up management of facilities, etc.;
9. Other matters prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
③ The profit ratio of a housing construction business operator under Article 7 (1) 5 of the Act shall not exceed six percent of total project costs. Total project costs shall be the sum of site acquisition costs, site-related charges, development costs, infrastructure installation costs, direct labor costs, relocation measure costs, sales expenses, general management expenses, capital costs and other expenses.
④ Notwithstanding Article 13-2 (2), a housing construction business operator under Article 7 (1) 5 of the Act may receive priority supply of developed housing sites within the scope of its investment share in accordance with its agreement with the public project implementer.
⑤ Matters necessary for selecting housing construction business operators other than those prescribed in paragraphs ① and ② shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

Article 6-5 (Entrustment of implementation of housing site development projects)
① The scope of housing site development projects that a public project implementer may have a housing construction business operator perform on its behalf under Article 7 (2) of the Act shall be:
1. Detailed design;
2. Site development works;
3. Infrastructure works;
4. Sale of developed housing sites.
② A housing construction business operator intending to perform part of a housing site development project on behalf of a public project implementer under Article 7 (2) of the Act shall submit an application for entrusted implementation accompanied by documents determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, specifying:
1. Name and address of the person performing the entrusted development project (for a corporation, its name and the name of its representative);
2. Name, location and area of the housing site development district in which the project is to be implemented;
3. An outline of the implementation plan for entrusted development, including:
(a) Purpose of the project;
(b) Outline and type of the project;
(c) Project implementation period.
③ Where a public project implementer intends to have a housing construction business operator implement a housing site development project on its behalf under Article 7 (2) of the Act, it shall enter into a contract for entrusted implementation with that operator.

Article 7 (Establishment of housing site development plans)
① "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 8 (1) 5 of the Act means:
1. Name of the housing site development plan (hereinafter referred to as the "development plan");
2. Name and address of the project implementer and name of its representative;
3. Location and area of the land to be developed.
② When intending to establish a development plan, the designating authority may require a person proposing designation under Article 3-2 of the Act to submit, within a specified period:
1. Documents specifying matters under Article 8 (1) 1 through 4 of the Act and the subparagraphs of paragraph ① of this Article;
2. A plan depicting the development plan on a topographic or cadastral map at a scale of at least 1:5,000.
③ Where necessary to establish a development plan, the designating authority may require a project implementer under Article 7 (1) 5 of the Act to submit the agreement concluded under Article 6-4 (2).
④ A land use plan under Article 8 (1) 3 of the Act shall include plans for housing construction sites and public facility sites as follows: <Amended on 2022.12.6>
1. Housing construction site plan: A plan for land to construct housing (classified as detached housing and multi-unit housing) and neighborhood living facilities (meaning facilities under subparagraphs 3 and 4 of attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act; hereinafter the same shall apply). Land for neighborhood living facilities shall be used only to construct neighborhood living facilities, kindergartens under the Regulations on Establishment and Operation of Schools of Various Levels below High School (hereinafter referred to as "kindergartens") and childcare centers under the Child Care Act (hereinafter referred to as "childcare centers").
2. Public facility site plan: A plan for land to install public facilities. Land for kindergartens, childcare centers or both shall permit construction of facilities in the following manner:
(a) On land for kindergartens, at least 70 percent of the total building floor area shall be allocated to a kindergarten, and the remaining area may be used for:
  (1) Childcare centers;
  (2) Private teaching institutes for minors falling under items (a) through (d) among courses of instruction in attached Table 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Establishment and Operation of Private Teaching Institutes and Extracurricular Lessons:
    (a) Institutes teaching computers;
    (b) Institutes teaching bookkeeping, abacus, mental arithmetic or speed reading;
    (c) Institutes teaching music, fine arts, dance or public speaking;
    (d) Reading rooms.
(b) On land for childcare centers, at least 60 percent of total building floor area shall be allocated to a childcare center, and the remaining area shall be used for:
  (1) Child-only facilities under Article 52 (1) 7 of the Child Welfare Act;
  (2) Children's libraries under Article 4 (2) 1 (b) of the Libraries Act.
(c) On land for kindergartens and childcare centers, at least 70 percent of the total building floor area shall be allocated to a kindergarten or childcare center or both, and the remaining area may be used for:
  (1) Private teaching institutes for minors falling under items (a) through (d) among courses of instruction in attached Table 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Establishment and Operation of Private Teaching Institutes and Extracurricular Lessons:
    (a) Institutes teaching computers;
    (b) Institutes teaching bookkeeping, abacus, mental arithmetic or speed reading;
    (c) Institutes teaching music, fine arts, dance or public speaking;
    (d) Reading rooms;
  (2) Child-only facilities under Article 52 (1) 7 of the Child Welfare Act;
  (3) Children's libraries under Article 4 (2) 1 (b) of the Libraries Act.
⑤ Matters necessary for standards for establishing housing site development plans other than those prescribed in paragraphs ① through ④ shall be separately determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

Article 8 (Preparation and approval of implementation plans)
① Where a project implementer prepares an implementation plan for housing site development projects under Article 9 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as an "implementation plan"), it shall include the matters specified in the subparagraphs of paragraphs ② and ③.
② A project implementer other than the designating authority seeking approval of an implementation plan under Article 9 (1) of the Act shall submit to the designating authority an application for approval of the implementation plan specifying:
1. Project implementation site;
2. Type and name of the project;
3. Name and address of the project implementer and name of its representative;
4. Period of implementation, including the time required for each construction phase.
③ The following documents shall be attached to the application under paragraph ②. The designating authority shall verify the cadastral map of the implementation site through the joint use of administrative information under Article 36 (1) of the Electronic Government Act:
1. Financing plan, including annual fund investment and procurement plans;
2. Location map of the project site;
3. Planned layout drawings and preliminary design documents;
4. List and disposal plan of public facilities, etc. under Article 25 of the Act;
5. Purchase and compensation plan for land, objects or rights (hereinafter referred to as "land, etc.");
6. Where land, etc. will be expropriated or used (hereinafter referred to as "expropriated"), documents specifying the location, lot number, land category, area, ownership and other rights and names and addresses of owners and rights holders, limited to particulars differing from the development plan under Article 8 (1) 4 of the Act;
7. A housing site supply plan specifying the location and area of land to be supplied, recipients or methods of selecting recipients, timing, methods and conditions of supply and methods for determining supply prices, together with maps dividing housing sites by purpose and recipient under the land use plan in Article 8 (1) 3 of the Act;
8. An agreement under Article 6-4 (2), limited to implementers under Article 7 (1) 5 of the Act.
④ When intending to prepare or approve an implementation plan under paragraph ①, the designating authority (excluding a Special Self-Governing Province Governor) shall hear opinions of the heads of relevant Sis, Guns or autonomous Gus: Provided, That this shall not apply where the project implementer has already consulted with them.
⑤ "Changes to minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 9 (1) of the Act means changes satisfying the following requirements:
1. An increase or decrease of no more than ten percent in project costs;
2. A decrease of no more than ten percent in the project area;
3. Changes to the installation of equipment or facilities within approved project costs.
⑥ Where any matter under the subparagraphs of paragraph ⑤ arises, the project implementer shall report it to the designating authority without delay.
⑦ When publicly notifying an implementation plan under Article 9 (3) and (4) of the Act, the designating authority shall specify:
1. Name of the project;
2. Name and address of the implementer and name of its representative;
3. Purpose and outline of the project;
4. Project implementation period;
5. Location and area of the project site;
6. Methods of public notice by publication of documents for interested parties under Article 21 (2) of the Act;
7. Location, lot number, land category, area, ownership and other rights in land, etc. to be expropriated, and names and addresses of owners and rights holders: Provided, That these particulars may be omitted where identical to those in the development plan publicly notified under Article 3 (6) of the Act, but the intention to omit them shall be specified;
8. Matters concerning district-unit plans under statutes on national land planning and utilization.
⑧ "Cases where special grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree exist" in Article 9 (5) of the Act means a housing site development district falling under any of the following:
1. An area already determined and publicly notified as an urban development zone for implementing an urban development project by a land substitution method under Section 3 of Chapter III of the Urban Development Act (hereinafter referred to in this Article as the "land substitution method") when designated as a housing site development district;
2. An area where land prices are significantly higher than those in nearby housing site development districts, making development very difficult except by the land substitution method;
3. A district containing numerous clustered settlements, buildings, etc., where implementation by the land substitution method or a mixed method under Article 21 (1) of the Urban Development Act is deemed necessary in consideration of relocation and livelihood measures for residents and other characteristics of the project district.
⑨ Where an urban or Gun management plan is deemed determined under Article 11 (1) 1 of the Act, the head of the relevant Si or Gun shall take necessary steps, including applying for approval of topographical maps of the implementation plan site under Article 32 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act, and the project implementer shall submit maps, etc. required for their public notification to the head of the Si or Gun.
⑩ Upon receiving an application for approval of an implementation plan from a project implementer under paragraph ②, the designating authority shall determine whether to grant approval within 60 days and notify the implementer.

Article 9 (Period for submitting opinions in response to consultation requests)
"Period prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 11 (2) of the Act means 20 days.

Article 9-2 (Ratio of housing sites used by public project implementers)
① "Land exceeding the ratio prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 12 (5) of the Act means land accounting for at least 30 percent of the total area of a housing site development district. The land used by a public project implementer as housing sites shall include at least a proportion of the total land area equal to the proportion of land expropriated within that district.
② The ratio of housing sites used by a public project implementer and housing construction business operator shall be determined in consideration of the respective ratios of land area secured by each party relative to the total district area, with details prescribed by agreement.
③ Notwithstanding paragraph ②, where a public project implementer uses as housing sites some of the land corresponding to the ratio of land secured by a housing construction business operator under Article 12 (5) of the Act, settlement of expenses shall be based on the following amount, with details prescribed by agreement:

Officially assessed land price of land acquired by the housing construction business operator × (Compensation for land expropriated by the public project implementer ÷ Officially assessed land price of land expropriated by the public project implementer) × (Area of land, from the operator's acquired share, used as housing sites by the public project implementer ÷ Area of land acquired by the housing construction business operator).

Article 9-3 (Retention of buildings, etc.)
① "Cases meeting requirements prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 12-2 (1) of the Act means any of the following:
1. All of the following requirements are met:
(a) Buildings, business premises, etc. have obtained authorization or permission, etc. under relevant statutes;
(b) The buildings, etc. are acceptable under the land use plan of the relevant project district;
(c) Retaining the buildings, etc. is substantially beneficial in terms of public interest or economic efficiency;
(d) The buildings, etc. are expected to be utilized over the long term even after completion of the relevant housing site development project.
2. The head of a relevant administrative agency, including a local government, requests retention on the ground that the buildings, etc. have cultural or artistic value, following deliberation by the Central Urban Planning Committee or a local urban planning committee under the National Land Planning and Utilization Act.
② "Public facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 12-2 (2) of the Act means public facilities transferred without compensation to the relevant management authority under Article 65 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act.
③ Where a project implementer requires the owner of facilities retained under Article 12-2 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "retained facilities") to pay part of the expenses necessary for installing public facilities, etc. under paragraph (2) of that Article (hereinafter referred to as "facility contributions"), methods for calculating and imposing facility contributions and eligibility for exemptions shall be as specified in attached Table 1. <Amended on 2017.12.5>
④ When disclosing the development cost of housing sites under Article 18-2 of the Act, a project implementer may disclose the details of facility contributions for the relevant project district. <Newly Inserted on 2021.4.20>

Article 10 (Repurchase price)
"Amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 13 (1) of the Act means legal interest accruing from the date of payment of compensation until the date of repurchase.

Article 11 Deleted. <2001.7.18>

Article 11-2 (Completion inspection)
① A project implementer seeking a completion inspection under Article 16 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for completion inspection to the designating authority accompanied by:
1. A statement of construction completion;
2. As-built layout and area calculation drawings recognized by the head of the relevant Si or Gun;
3. Statements and plans of land area by use;
4. A statement of the area of developed land by owner;
5. A statement and drawings of the transfer of public facilities, etc. under Article 25 of the Act;
6. A comparison drawing of old and new cadastral records;
7. Other documents prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
② Where the designating authority recognizes that the housing site development project has been completed in accordance with the implementation plan approved under Article 9 of the Act, it shall issue a completion inspection certificate to the project implementer and publicly announce completion in the Official Gazette.
③ When publicly announcing completion under paragraph ②, the following shall be specified:
1. Name of the project;
2. Name and address of the project implementer and name of its representative;
3. Location of the project site;
4. Total area of the project site and area by use;
5. Date of completion;
6. Matters concerning management and disposal of major facilities.

Article 12 (Entrustment of land purchase duties, etc.)
① Where a project implementer other than a local government intends to entrust land purchase and compensation for losses under Article 17 (1) of the Act, it shall submit to the relevant Special Metropolitan Mayor, Metropolitan Mayor, Do Governor, Special Self-Governing Province Governor or the head of the relevant Si or Gun a written document specifying the subject of entrustment and conditions thereof.
② Where land purchase and compensation for losses are entrusted under Article 17 (2) of the Act, rates of entrustment fees to be paid by the project implementer shall be as specified in attached Table 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects.

Article 13 Deleted. <2007.7.30>

Article 13-2 (Methods for supplying housing sites)
① A project implementer shall classify housing sites developed by the implementer into land for constructing housing of national housing size under Article 2, subparagraph 6 of the Housing Act (including rental housing; hereinafter referred to as "land for housing of national housing size"), other housing construction land, and land for public facilities under Article 2, subparagraph 2 of the Act. Except for land for public facilities, priority shall be given to supplying land for housing of national housing size. <Amended on 2016.8.11>
② Where a project implementer supplies housing sites under Article 18 (1) of the Act, it shall determine prices in advance, then select recipients and sell or lease the sites. Prices may differ according to use, region and recipient to facilitate urban development and the smooth supply and demand of housing sites. Where housing sites under paragraph ⑤ 1 are supplied subject to the condition under paragraph ③ 2, advance determination of prices may be omitted. <Amended on 2021.4.20, 2021.12.28>
③ When selecting recipients for supply under paragraph ②, the implementer shall conduct competitive bidding subject to either of the following conditions: Provided, That supply may be conducted by lottery where necessary in consideration of the use of the site, recipients, etc. <Amended on 2021.4.20>
1. When supplying land for multi-unit housing, part of the housing to be constructed on the land shall be sold to the implementer for use as public rental housing under Article 2, subparagraph 1 (a) of the Special Act on Public Housing;
2. The land shall be developed through the establishment of a publicly offered real estate investment trust under Article 49-3 of the Real Estate Investment Company Act (including a real estate investment company scheduled to offer shares publicly under Article 14-8 (1) and (2) of that Act), or a real estate collective investment scheme under Article 229, subparagraph 2 of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act (excluding private collective investment schemes under Article 9 (19) of that Act).
④ When selecting recipients under the main sentence of paragraph ③, the implementer shall follow procedures and methods determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on 2021.4.20>

⑤ Notwithstanding paragraphs ② through ④, a project implementer may supply the following housing sites by competitive bidding: <Newly Inserted on 2021.4.20, 2021.12.28>
1. Housing sites to be used for profit-making activities, including sites for sales facilities, as determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
2. Housing sites other than land for constructing multi-unit housing under project plans approved under Article 15 of the Housing Act: Provided, That this shall not apply where necessary to stabilize land prices or achieve public purposes.
⑥ Where housing sites supplied under paragraphs ② through ⑤ are sites for specific facilities, such as schools or medical facilities, prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, the implementer may restrict the qualifications of recipients. <Newly Inserted on 2021.4.20>
⑦ Notwithstanding paragraphs ③ through ⑤, a project implementer may supply housing sites by negotiated contract in any of the following cases: Provided, That where the quantity applied for under subparagraph 4 exceeds the quantity planned in the development plan, supply shall be by lottery. Where sites are supplied to persons transferring land they owned before designation of a development-restricted zone under the Special Act on Designation and Management of Development-Restricted Zones (hereinafter referred to as a "development-restricted zone"), or acquired by inheritance after such designation, within a housing site development district designated in that zone, the sites may be supplied preferentially according to criteria prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport. <Amended on 2014.7.21, 2014.7.28, 2015.11.11, 2015.12.22, 2016.8.11, 2017.1.17, 2021.4.20, 2021.12.28, 2025.10.1>
1. Where sites are supplied to the State, a local government or a public institution prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport among project entities under the Housing Act;
1-2. Where land for construction of rental housing is supplied to a real estate investment company under Article 2, subparagraph 1 of the Real Estate Investment Company Act in which the following persons, individually or jointly, have contributed more than 50 percent of the total equity:
(a) The State;
(b) Local governments;
(c) Korea Land and Housing Corporation under the Korea Land and Housing Corporation Act;
(d) Local public corporations established for housing projects under Article 49 of the Local Public Enterprises Act;
2. Where sites for public facilities not eligible for sale to the general public, including roads, schools, parks and public offices, are supplied to the State, local governments or other persons legally authorized to install the relevant public facilities;
3. Where sites within the minimum extent required to maintain or manage buildings or other facilities in a housing site development district that are to remain in place under the implementation plan publicly notified pursuant to Article 9 (3) of the Act are supplied;
4. Where sites of a scale prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport are supplied to a person who agrees to negotiations under the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects and transfers all land owned by that person within the housing site development district to the project implementer (limited, in a Seoul metropolitan area under the Seoul Metropolitan Area Readjustment Planning Act, to land of at least the area prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport; including objects or rights under Article 3 of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects, if any). The person shall have owned the land for at least one year before the date of announcement under Article 5 (2); this shall include persons who acquired all land from its former owner within the district after the date one year before that announcement, and persons who acquired land by court judgment or inheritance;
5. Where a housing construction business operator registered under Article 4 of the Housing Act transfers to the project implementer, through negotiations under the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects, all land owned within the housing site development district as of the announcement under Article 5 (2) (including land under an agreement to transfer ownership as of that date for which ownership is acquired by the date of designation of the district) and sites are supplied to the operator within the area prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport in consideration of the purposes of ownership, uses of land and progress of the housing construction project: Provided, That for land subject to agreements to transfer ownership as of the announcement date, the relevant agreement must be demonstrated to have undergone any of the following before that date:
(a) Certification of the agreement under Article 3 of the Act on Special Measures for Registration of Real Estate;
(b) Reporting of the real estate transaction under Article 3 of the Act on Report on Real Estate Transactions, etc.;
(c) Preparation of a notarized deed under Articles 25 through 35, 35-2 and 36 through 40 of the Notary Public Act;
(d) Authentication of a private document under Articles 57, 57-2, 58 and 59 of the Notary Public Act;
6. Where a housing association established with authorization under Article 11 of the Housing Act to construct housing in a housing site development district has acquired, as of the announcement under Article 5 (2), at least one half of the land necessary to construct housing to be supplied to its members and transfers all such land to the project implementer through negotiations under the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects, and sites within an area prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport are supplied to the association;
7. Where sites are supplied to persons selected under procedures and methods determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport because development through special design (meaning design undertaken where it is necessary to adopt creative development proposals through a design competition or develop land for multiple uses, etc.) is required for the desirable development of a city;
8. Where an industrial complex under the Industrial Sites and Development Act with an area of at least one million square meters meeting either of the following conditions is established within a Si or Gun containing a housing site development district of at least 3,300,000 square meters; a project implementer of the industrial complex (including an enterprise that establishes a factory after acquiring at least 50 percent of industrial facility sites within the complex) requires land for employee housing construction, schools, etc.; the head of the relevant Si or Gun and the Minister of Trade and Industry recommend the supply; and the Housing Policy Deliberation Committee under Article 8 of the Framework Act on Residence recognizes the necessity of supplying housing sites, within an area prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport:
(a) An industrial complex established by an enterprise relocating from the Seoul metropolitan area under Article 2, subparagraph 1 of the Seoul Metropolitan Area Readjustment Planning Act to an area outside it;
(b) An industrial complex established to construct factories of high-tech business categories prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
9. Where sites within an area prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport are supplied to a person entitled to compensation in land under Article 63 (1) 1 of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects, considering efficient use of housing sites, etc.;
10. Where sites within an area prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport are supplied to a development-specialized real estate investment company receiving in-kind contributions under Article 26-3 (1) of the Real Estate Investment Company Act, considering efficient use of housing sites, etc.;
11. Other cases where supply by negotiated contract is permitted under relevant statutes.
⑧ A project implementer intending to supply housing sites shall publicly announce the following, except where recipient qualifications are restricted under paragraph ⑥ or sites are supplied by negotiated contract under paragraph ⑦: <Amended on 2021.4.20>
1. Name and address of the implementer and name of its representative;
2. Location, area and purpose of the housing site (including the details of any prohibitions or restrictions on uses);
3. Timing, methods and conditions of supply;
4. Supply price;
5. Housing site development cost prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
6. Period and location for applications;
7. Eligibility for application;
8. Documents required when applying.
⑨ Where deemed necessary to stabilize the residential lives of citizens, including promoting the supply of national housing, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may determine criteria for housing site supply methods and prices by purpose, region and housing size under Article 18 (2) of the Act and require prices to be determined accordingly. <Amended on 2021.4.20>

Article 13-3 (Special provisions concerning restrictions on resale of housing sites)
"Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 19-2 (1) of the Act means any of the following cases where consent of the project implementer has been obtained: Provided, That subparagraphs 1, 2, 7 and 9-3 shall apply only to persons initially supplied housing sites by the project implementer. <Amended on 2008.2.29, 2008.8.12, 2008.11.26, 2009.6.25, 2011.8.30, 2013.1.9, 2013.3.23, 2015.8.11, 2016.8.11, 2017.12.29, 2020.7.7, 2021.2.17, 2021.4.20, 2021.12.28, 2023.11.28, 2025.6.25>
